The first term can be written as $a = \frac{2}{3} = \frac{2\sqrt{3}}{3\sqrt{3}} = \frac{2\sqrt{3}}{3} \cdot \frac{1}{\sqrt{3}} = \frac{2\sqrt{3}}{3} \cdot \frac{\sqrt{3}}{3} = -\frac{\sqrt{3}{3}} \cdot \sqrt{3}$.

Hence, option C.
