We know that the diagonals differ by 6 units, so we can write the equation:
$$d_1 - d_2 = 6$$

We also know that the diagonals of a rhombus are perpendicular bisectors of each other, and the side length of the rhombus is $\sqrt{89}$ units. This means that each right-angled triangle formed by the diagonals has a hypotenuse equal to $\sqrt{89}$ units.

