Similarly, substituting $x = 1$ into the polynomial, we get $f(1) = 1^2 + b \cdot 1 + c = 1 + b + c = 10$. 

Substituting $c = 4$ into the equation $1 + b + c = 10$, we get $1 + b + 4 = 10$, which simplifies to $b = 5$. 

Therefore, the polynomial $f(x)$ is $x^2 + 5x + 4$. 

